Subject: menu-v2: a menu that has never opened is its trigger alone until a pointer or focus reaches it

What: MenuV2's root keeps a small context of its own. MenuV2.Trigger draws its element
as Kobalte's Button with the closed trigger's attributes (id, aria-haspopup,
aria-expanded="false", data-closed) and MenuV2.Portal only registers its children.
The trigger's first pointerenter or focusin, or an open prop, mounts Kobalte's
DropdownMenu beside the children: its trigger is spread onto the same element through
adoptElement and the registered portal renders inside its context. Pointerenter and
focusin precede every pointerdown and keydown that opens a menu, so Kobalte handles
the real press itself. ContextMenu is unchanged.
Why: every closed DropdownMenu in the composer, the rail and the review and task rows
built Kobalte's menu root, its trigger handlers and a focus listener at mount.

